    "IFS sessions work with specific internal parts directly -- the anxious part, the angry part, the avoidant part, the part that carries old pain. For San Leandro clients dealing with anger or anxiety that has been present for years, this means working with parts that developed protective responses in real circumstances and helping those parts understand that the current environment can be navigated differently. The work is respectful of what those parts were built for and focused on helping the internal system update rather than forcing change through willpower.",
    "EMDR sessions process specific experiences or accumulated patterns of experience the nervous system has not fully integrated. The bilateral stimulation activates natural processing capacity that allows stored responses to update. For San Leandro clients dealing with complex or accumulated adversity rather than single-incident trauma, the processing unfolds across multiple sessions working through layers of experience systematically. Most clients find it more manageable than expected because the work does not require extensive verbal narration of difficult material.",
