    "IFS sessions build trust at the pace trust actually builds rather than assuming it from the start. Early sessions focus on understanding what the internal parts developed in response to, what each part has been protecting, and what the system actually needs rather than what it has been told it should need. For Richmond clients whose experience with systems and institutions has given them good reasons for skepticism, this approach -- working with the internal system rather than imposing a framework on it -- often feels meaningfully different from previous experiences with mental health care.",
