  h1: "Depression Therapy in San Francisco, CA | IFS & EMDR for Lasting Relief",
  intro: "Depression therapy in San Francisco, CA using IFS and EMDR -- for high-functioning depression, chronic low mood, burnout-related depression, and the particular emptiness that accumulates when a person has built a successful life and finds it returning less than expected. San Francisco produces a specific depression profile that is worth naming precisely. It is not the kind that keeps people in bed. It is the kind that keeps people fully functional while feeling increasingly hollow -- meeting every deadline, maintaining every relationship, showing up to everything, and experiencing almost none of it as genuinely meaningful. That presentation is one of the most common and most undertreated in the city, and it responds directly to IFS and EMDR.",
  localContent: "Marcus Ghiasi is a Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist offering depression treatment to San Francisco adults via telehealth. San Francisco's performance culture creates a specific barrier to addressing depression -- the same culture that produces high-functioning depression makes it difficult to acknowledge because acknowledging it feels like admitting that the performance is insufficient. Depression therapy here takes that dynamic seriously from the first session rather than treating it as something to set aside to get to the real work. Sessions are Wednesday through Friday from anywhere in California. IFS works with the internal parts maintaining the depressive state directly. EMDR processes the specific experiences that initiated or deepened the depression at the neurological level. SF residents access sessions from home or office without commuting. A free 15-minute consultation is the starting point.",
