    "The relationship between professional identity and self-worth is one of the most common underlying dynamics in Menlo Park therapy. When a person's sense of who they are is built substantially on what they do and how well they do it, any disruption to professional status -- a bad quarter, a failed raise, a company pivot, a career transition -- produces a psychological response that is disproportionate to the external event. Individual therapy works with the parts that built that identity structure, understanding what they were protecting and what would need to be true for worth to rest on something more stable.",
