    "IFS sessions involve turning toward specific internal parts with curiosity rather than judgment. The anxious part, the self-critical part, the avoidant part, the part that carries old pain from earlier experiences. Rather than discussing these parts from a narrative distance, IFS builds a direct relationship with each -- understanding what it is protecting and what it needs. For Novato clients dealing with anxiety or trauma that has not responded to previous approaches, this direct engagement with the internal system is often what produces movement.",
    "EMDR sessions are structured around specific experiences or clusters of experiences the nervous system has not fully processed. The bilateral stimulation -- eye movements or tapping -- activates natural processing in a way that allows stored threat responses to update. For Novato veterans, first responders, and anyone whose anxiety or PTSD has roots in specific traumatic experiences, EMDR often produces significant change in fewer sessions than insight-oriented approaches typically require because it works at the neurological level rather than the narrative one.",
