    "EMDR sessions are structured around specific experiences or clusters of experiences the nervous system has not fully processed. For Petaluma and Sonoma County residents whose anxiety, depression, or PTSD has roots in wildfire trauma, loss, or other specific events, EMDR provides a structured path through difficult material that does not require extensive verbal narration. The bilateral stimulation activates natural processing capacity in a way that allows stored responses to update. Most clients notice meaningful change faster than they expected because the work happens at the neurological level rather than the narrative one.",
